+// SSL_verify_peer_cert_chain performs the built-in X.509 verification
+// procedure on the current peer chain, including any X.509 verification
+// callbacks, without modifying the session. Unlike normal handshakes, this
+// explicitly requested check is strict even with SSL_VERIFY_NONE. Returns
+// X509_V_OK on acceptance or the X509_V_ERR_* code on failure. Call only when
+// no other verification of this connection is active. The native custom
+// verify callback is not invoked. No error queue entries from this check
+// remain on return.
+OPENSSL_EXPORT long SSL_verify_peer_cert_chain(SSL *ssl);
+
+
 
